> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> 
> */
. 
. * ============================
. * Data Preparation * 
. * ============================
. 
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
.         * biobirth contains information on fertility history
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", keep(1 3) keepus(kidpnr01 kid
> pnr02 kidgeb01 kidgeb02 kidsex01 kidsex02 kidmon01 kidmon02) nogen
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are c
> onsolidated from different sources
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", keep(1 3) keepus(pgpsbil pg
> famstd pgemplst pglabgro) nogen
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", keep(1 3) keepus(plh0308_v2 p
> lh0333 plh0004 pli0040 pli0043_h pli0044_h pli0046) nogen
(label cid_EN already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * hgen contains generated variables on household level from the house
> hold interview; use for household net income
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/bioparen.dta", keep(1 3) keepus(fsedu msedu)
>  nogen

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
.         label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
.         save "$DATA/h4_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h4_dataset.dta saved

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.  
.         keep if inrange(netto,10,19)
(143,471 observations deleted)

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         set seed 123

.         
.         *Change non valid/missing values to NA
.         mvdecode _all, mv(-1=. \ -2=.t \ -3=.x \ -5=.y \ -8=.z)
       parid: 165425 missing values generated
         sex: 13 missing values generated
     gebjahr: 4 missing values generated
     sampreg: 77 missing values generated
     casemat: 519473 missing values generated
     todjahr: 489691 missing values generated
     todinfo: 489691 missing values generated
    immiyear: 428898 missing values generated
     corigin: 330 missing values generated
    gebmonat: 8942 missing values generated
     loc1989: 54098 missing values generated
     locinfo: 17530 missing values generated
 birthregion: 280794 missing values generated
birthregio~w: 286720 missing values generated
    arefback: 598 missing values generated
    arefinfo: 598 missing values generated
       rv_id: 399031 missing values generated
    kidpnr01: 253279 missing values generated
    kidpnr02: 316414 missing values generated
    kidgeb01: 140513 missing values generated
    kidgeb02: 244431 missing values generated
    kidsex01: 140360 missing values generated
    kidsex02: 244499 missing values generated
    kidmon01: 276010 missing values generated
    kidmon02: 330431 missing values generated
    pgfamstd: 2315 missing values generated
    pglabgro: 217158 missing values generated
    pgemplst: 29 missing values generated
     pgpsbil: 14944 missing values generated
     plh0004: 428081 missing values generated
  plh0308_v2: 490191 missing values generated
     plh0333: 470787 missing values generated
     pli0040: 26962 missing values generated
   pli0043_h: 21018 missing values generated
   pli0044_h: 27097 missing values generated
     pli0046: 52431 missing values generated
       fsedu: 67229 missing values generated
       msedu: 65834 missing values generated

. 
.         *Recode gender
.         gen male=(sex==1)

. 
.         *Generate age and age²
.         gen age=piyear-gebjahr
(4 missing values generated)

.         replace age=syear-gebjahr if missing(age)
(0 real changes made)

.         gen age2= age^2
(4 missing values generated)

. 
.         *Generate education dummy
.         gen abitur=0 if pgpsbil>0

.         replace abitur=1 if pgpsbil==4
(105,487 real changes made)

. 
.         *Define daughter dummy
.         gen daughter=(kidsex01==2) 

.         
.         *Generate parents education dummy
.         gen parent_abitur=(fsedu==4) | (msedu==4)

.         
.         *Define labor income
.         gen labor_earn=pglabgro
(217,158 missing values generated)

.         replace labor_earn=0 if pglabgro<0
(0 real changes made)

.         
.         *Recode political attitudes (voting outcome)
.         replace plh0333=29 if plh0333==-5 & inrange(psample,17,19)
(0 real changes made)

.         clonevar party_vote=plh0333
(475,949 missing values generated)

.         
.         *Define and standardize attitudes towards gender equality
.         sum plh0308_v2 if syear==2018

    Variable |        Obs        Mean    Std. dev.       Min        Max
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------
  plh0308_v2 |     24,299    5.451335    1.722319          1          7

.         gen equalityattitude=(plh0308_v2-r(mean))/r(sd)
(495,353 missing values generated)

. 
.         *Define dummies for first and second child
.         gen first_child18=1 if kidgeb01<=2018
(142,338 missing values generated)

.         gen second_child18=1 if kidgeb02<=2018
(246,761 missing values generated)

.         
.         
.         *** Sample restriction
.         
.         *Only keep if first child born before or in 2018 and no second child 
> at 2018
.         keep if first_child18==1 & second_child18!=1
(415,048 observations deleted)

. 
.         *Only keep cross section 2018
.         keep if syear==2018
(99,328 observations deleted)

. 
.         *Only keep if full information on following variables
.         keep if !missing(equalityattitude,age, daughter, migback, kidgeb01, a
> bitur, parent_abitur, party_vote, labor_earn, pgemplst )
(2,412 observations deleted)

. 
.         *Only keep if partner is also in sample (to allow for household fixed
>  effects)
.         *keep if !missing(parid)
.         *preserve
.         *keep parid
.         *rename parid pid
.         *tempfile parid
.         *save `parid' , replace
.         *restore
.         *merge 1:1 pid using `parid'
.         *keep if _merge==3 // only keep observations if we have all variables
>  from both partners.
.         *drop _merge
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * To identify the causal effect of having a daughter on support towar
> ds gender equality (as
.         * measured by attitudes), we estimate a cross-sectional OLS regressio
> n in a sample of parents
.         * who in 2018 only have exactly one child (first-born). Specifically,
>  we use the fact that the
.         * sex of the first-born child is random by nature for the identificat
> ion of the effect of having
.         * a daughter compared to having a son. Our dependent variable is surv
> eyed in 2018 and
.         * captures attitudes towards equal sharing of employment and care wor
> k within couples. The coefficient 
.         * of interest captures the interaction term between father/mother and
>  daughter/son. We
.         * include only individuals for whom we also have valid observations f
> or their partner, in order
.         * to account for household fixed effects.
. 
.         * CHANGED SPECIFICATION: In the PAP (as writte above) we wanted to co
> ntrol for household fixed effects. This
.         * can not be done, as the variable of interest (daughter) is constant
>  across households and would therefore
.         * be fully absorbed in the household fixed effects. For the regressio
> n model we corrected this and REMOVED
.         * the household fixed effects
. 
.         reg equalityattitude i.male##(i.daughter c.age c.age2 i.migback i.kid
> geb01 i.abitur i.parent_abitur i.party_vote c.labor_earn i.pgemplst), vce(clu
> ster hid)
